\\bar U\\) is disjoint from\n\\(f(D)\\).  Extend \\(q\\) to a map \\(A\\setminus U\\to A\\setminus F\\) by\nsetting \\(q(y)=y\\) for \\(y\\notin F\\).  Clearly, the extended map \\(q\\)\nis PL,  \\(g:=q\\circ f\\) is also PL, and \\(g\\) has the required properties.\\qed"
